    \section2 Qt Linguist
    \list
    \li lupdate now preserves the existing line endings in \c{.ts} files.
        On Windows, files with CRLF line endings are updated in-place
        with CRLF; files with LF line endings and new files keep LF.
    \li Qt Linguist has a new option -web-help to use online web documentation if desired.
    \endlist

    \section1 Platform Changes

    \section2 Build System Changes

    \list
      \li Building and using Qt now requires CMake 3.25 or later.
      \li Added the \c{static_compiler_runtime} CMake feature to statically
          link the C++ runtime libraries. On Windows (MSVC) this uses the
          Hybrid CRT method, removing the dependency on the Visual C++
          Redistributable.
      \li The following CMake API has been taken out of Technology Preview
          and is now fully supported:
          \l{qt_finalize_project}{qt_finalize_project()},
          \l{qt_extract_metatypes}{qt_extract_metatypes()},
          \l{qt_deploy_translations}{qt_deploy_translations()},
          \l{QT_TARGETS_FOLDER},
          \l{QT_RESOURCE_PREFIX},
          \l{QT_DEPLOY_SUPPORT}, and
          \l{QT_ENABLE_VERBOSE_DEPLOYMENT}.
      \li The \c{qt_no_entrypoint} target property has been renamed to
          \l{QT_NO_ENTRYPOINT}. The old name is still recognized for
          backward compatibility.
      \li Added CMake policy \c{QTP0006}. When set to \c{NEW},
          \l{qt_generate_wayland_protocol_client_sources}{qt_generate_wayland_protocol_client_sources()}
          and
          \l{qt_generate_wayland_protocol_server_sources}{qt_generate_wayland_protocol_server_sources()}
          default to
          \c{PRIVATE_CODE} instead of \c{PUBLIC_CODE}.
      \li \l{qt_add_shaders}{qt_add_shaders()} progress messages are now logged at
          \c{DEBUG} level instead of \c{NOTICE}, suppressing them from
          the default build output. Pass \c{--log-level=NOTICE} to
          CMake to restore the previous behaviour.
      \li \l{qt_add_qml_module}{qt_add_qml_module()} gained a \c{NO_GENERATE_QTCONF} option
          to suppress automatic \c{qt.conf} generation in the build
          directory.
      \li The build system now offers a <exe>_qmlpreview
          target for each executable with a QML module. When you "build" that
          target, the build system starts the \l qmlpreview utility with the correct
          arguments and allows you to QML-preview your executable. In particular
          it automatically resolves the .qrc file paths.
    \endlist

    \section2 Desktop Platforms

    \section3 Windows
    \list
    \endlist

