    \section3 macOS
    \list
      \li \l{QScreen::grabWindow()} now uses ScreenCaptureKit instead
          of the deprecated \c{CGDisplayCreateImageForRect}. A
          permission prompt will be shown the first time the API is
          used.
      \li \l{QWindow}{QWindows} parented into non-flipped
          \c{NSView}s now maintain their position relative to the
          superview's top-left corner when the superview is resized.
      \li \l{QCocoaNativeInterface::setEmbeddedInForeignView()} is no
          longer necessary or supported to embed a Qt view hierarchy
          in a foreign \c{NSView}. Qt now manages this automatically.
      \li Sandboxed apps built against a static Qt build
          are now relocatable by default on Apple platforms.
      \li \l{QMainWindow}'s unified title and toolbar mode is now
          implemented via \l{Qt::ExpandedClientAreaHint} and
          \l{Qt::NoTitleBarBackgroundHint} instead of the deprecated
          textured \c{NSWindow} style.
      \li \l{QStandardPaths::standardLocations()} now includes the
          system-wide \c{/Library/Preferences} directory for
          \c{ConfigLocation}, \c{GenericConfigLocation}, and
          \c{AppConfigLocation}.
    \endlist

