    \section3 iOS
    \list
      \li \l{QStandardPaths::PublicShareLocation} now returns
          \c{<APPROOT>/Public} (matching \c{NSSharedPublicDirectory})
          instead of the previously synthesized path inside the
          Documents directory.
      \li \l{QStandardPaths::standardLocations}{standardLocations}(\c{PicturesLocation})
          no longer contains a duplicate entry for the writable
          Documents/Pictures path.
      \li \l{QStandardPaths::TemplatesLocation} is now correctly
          reported as not supported on iOS, matching the existing
          documentation.
    \endlist

